From 97aaa5af867194873fd04273b9fc79614c9b73f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDNA4-MacOS contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] radv/darwin: keep physical heaps, budget only bounds Private
 max_allocation headroom

Mesa reports the physical pool totals and real usages; the kext's
per-session VRAM budget (ABI 1.10 reserved[3..7]) only bounds
vram.max_allocation (avail when valid, otherwise the real free bytes).
No shrinking of totals to the shared cap, no cap-avail fake usage, and
Private max is not bound to the visible 3/4 limit. ABI layout and minor
stay 1.10; per-session held bytes and the visible subcap are not
reported and must not be invented (see the header comments).

---
 include/darwin/rdna4_native_abi.h           | 19 ++++-
 src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_budget.h     | 69 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_drm.c        |  6 +-
 src/amd/common/darwin/test/acd_budget_test.c | 104 ++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 193 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_budget.h
 create mode 100644 src/amd/common/darwin/test/acd_budget_test.c

